---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { AUTHOR, GITHUB_URL } from '../consts';
// Edit the prose below freely. This is your page. Keep it in your own voice.
---

<Base title="About" description={`About ${AUTHOR}`}>
  <article class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>Hi, I'm {AUTHOR}.</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        I like running small, reproducible experiments on open-source and
        open-weight models: how they behave, where they break, and what happens
        when you probe them on safety as well as everyday tasks. Most of what I
        publish here runs locally on a laptop, with programmatic grading you can
        rerun yourself.
      </p>

      <p>
        {/* TODO: replace with your own bio. A few things you might add: */}
        {/* who you are, what you work on, why open models interest you, */}
        {/* how to reach you (email / social), and anything you want people */}
        {/* to know before they read the experiments. */}
        This page is a placeholder. Write whatever you want here: what draws you
        to open models, what you're currently poking at, and how to get in touch.
      </p>

      <p>
        The code for these experiments lives on
        <a href={GITHUB_URL} rel="me noopener" target="_blank">GitHub</a>.
        The ideas and experiments are mine, built with AI assistance.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="back mono"><a href="/">← all experiments</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  h1 { font-size: 2rem; margin: 0.3rem 0 1.2rem; }
  .back { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1.5rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
</style>
